ft8_lib — the FT8 and FT4 coding, by Kārlis Goba, YL3JG.

    https://github.com/kgoba/ft8_lib        MIT licence, see LICENSE

These are the files of the library's ft8/ folder as they are in zbitxv2,
which has had them since 2022. They are not changed here. The one thing in
them that is not the library's own is in decode.c: get_snr(), and the snr
that ft8_find_sync() puts in each candidate, which were added in zbitxv2.

    constants   the Costas pattern, the Gray map, the LDPC matrices
    crc         the 14 bit check on a message
    ldpc        the error correction: belief propagation
    decode      finds where the signals are in a slot and reads them
    unpack      turns the 77 bits of a message into its text
    text        the alphabets of callsigns and grids
    pack        turns a text into its 77 bits       (for transmitting)
    encode      turns the 77 bits into the 79 tones (for transmitting)

The library's own example, decode_ft8.c, is where modems/ft8_monitor.c
comes from. The library used its own copy of kiss_fft; the radio has
kiss_fft already, in dsp/kiss_fft, and that one is used.

They are built on their own with their warnings off, as kiss_fft is, so
that the warnings shown are all the radio's own.
